Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:51:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: opp: sun50i: Allow turbo-mode and opp-suspend

The Allwinner H6/A100/H616 OPP binding lists the properties an OPP node
may have and rejects all others, so a board cannot mark an OPP as a
boost frequency (turbo-mode) or as the frequency to use while
suspending (opp-suspend). Both are generic properties defined by
opp-v2-base.yaml, and the cpufreq-dt driver honours them.

Allow them, so that a board can, for example, keep its fastest OPP as
a boost frequency that is off by default.

This patch was drafted with an AI coding assistant (Claude) and checked
with dt_binding_check, and with dtbs_check on an H616 board whose OPP
table uses both properties (rejected before this patch, accepted after).
---
Notes (below the cut, not part of the commit):
- No board in the tree uses these properties in an Allwinner OPP table
  yet. The intended user is the Anbernic RG34XX SP (H700), whose
  downstream table keeps 1512 MHz as a boost OPP; [TODO before sending:
  link the board series that uses them, or drop this patch until one
  exists, since a binding change without a user is often refused].
- [TODO before sending: add the hardware test, if any.]

 .../bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml      | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
index 75ab552f6e..2aa53d7249 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@ patternProperties:
       opp-hz: true
       clock-latency-ns: true
       opp-microvolt: true
+      opp-suspend: true
+      turbo-mode: true
       opp-supported-hw:
         maxItems: 1
         description:

